<!--Workspace Documentation — LinkingRules
  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation.LinkingRules-->
<wsdocumentation:LinkingRules xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:core="org.blockml.bml.core"
  xmlns:wsdocumentation="com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.documentation">

  <baseType>
    core:Documentation
  </baseType>
  <is>
    Normative monorepo BML linking and SSOT rules
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Normative rules for this monorepo:

    1. Workspace to packages only. The workspace Library may list package
       libraries in dependencies. Package Library files must never depend on
       com.machineblocks.bml.renderer.workspace.Library.
    2. No re-export. Package block files stay under packages/*/blocks/. The hub
       file tree contains only workspace orientation blocks.
    3. Package SSOT. Each publishable package owns its BML under packages/*/blocks/
       and points at it via package.json blockml.library.
    4. Hub SSOT. The root package.json blockml.library points at this workspace
       Library.
    5. Dependency direction. The render target depends on the block render
       engine and peers @machineblocks/core. The consuming project depends on
       @machineblocks/core. The CLI may depend on the render target, on
       @blockml/cli, and on @machineblocks/core. The engine must not depend on
       MachineBlocks packages.
    6. Domain SSOT stays outside. Native parameters, type shapes, and the SCAD
       library are @machineblocks/core. This repo specifies how a compiler target
       emits SCAD from that model.
    7. Rename. Do not reintroduce the names maker-engine, MakerEngine,
       @blockml/engine-maker, or @machineblocks/machineblocks-v3-scad-target.
       Registry id machineblocks-v3-scad remains.

  </documentation>
  <references>
    <see type="wsdocumentation:TransferredSources" relation="ReadNext" />
    <see type="wsdocumentation:Introduction" relation="SeeAlso" />
  </references>
</wsdocumentation:LinkingRules>
